  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Capacity of National and Regional Actors to Respond to Climate Related Security Risks</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed joint programme between IOM and WFP aims to strengthen the capacity of the Government of Iraq (GoI) and regional authorities [1] to understand and strategically respond to existing and emerging climate-related security risks through an integrated, human-security approach that focuses on both prevention, mitigation and response. At the national level, the programme will conduct a climate security risk assessment to identify anthropogenic and naturally induced risks that threaten human security in relation to climate change. At the regional level, the programme will facilitate social integration into host communities of climate-induced displaced persons from Iraq&#x2019;s southern governorates through a participatory approach centered on the engagement of populations experiencing multidimensional vulnerabilities such as water scarcity and security, displacement and forced migration, extreme weather events from climate variability, and others. The key results expected following the implementation of the programme are: 1) creation of a roadmap on the formulation of GoI climate security policy and implementation plan, informed by the climate risk security assessment; and 2) downscaled action plans within targeted governorates and district level on climate security and reintegration plan for affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
